# Transient state. These exist ONLY while something is waiting for a reset and
# are deleted the moment it completes — their absence is the healthy state.
pending-resume.json
pending-sessions.json
.session-rescue.lock

# Ledger of handled (sessionId, limit-time) pairs. Machine-local, and session
# ids are not worth publishing.
resumed-sessions.json

# Logs. These matter most: the wrapper appends Claude's own stdout, so the log
# accumulates whatever you were actually working on — drafts, file contents,
# private project material. Never commit one.
*.log

# Written into a rescued project's folder; if one ever lands here, it is noise.
QUOTAWAKE-RESUMED.md

# Claude Code per-machine settings: absolute paths and a personal allowlist.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Scratch folders from live end-to-end tests.
.livetest*/

# The original internal handoff note. Its content lives on, scrubbed, in
# DESIGN-NOTES.md; this copy is kept locally only because it also records
# machine specifics and home paths that should not be published. Safe to delete.
remote-control-keepawake-handoff.md
